				"source_en": "Incisional block following ovariohysterectomy (extra-label): 5.4 mg/kg diluted to 5 mL with 0.9% NaCl into a syringe with a 22-gauge, 1-inch needle; after linea alba closure 2.5 mL was injected under the rectus sheath in a continuous line on both sides of the incision. After closure of the subcutaneous layer the remaining 2.5 mL was slowly injected at least 5 mm away from the incision such that a continuous line of anesthetic extended around the entire incision. Pain scores remained low for up to 68 hours after surgery, and reduced the need for postoperative robenacoxib use."
